    {
      "caption": "Four prespecified claims with their mean margin gaps and simultaneous one-sided lower bounds. For nonlinear comparisons the gap is 0.97 times comparator loss minus candidate loss; for linear noninferiority it is 1.05 times ridge loss minus KAHM loss. The paired-t bounds use 24 independent repetition aggregates and Bonferroni family allocation 0.05/4. The plotted values divide absolute SMSE margin gaps by the observed mean comparator SMSE and multiply by 100 for legibility. This display rescaling does not change the sign or the claim decision and is not a risk-ratio confidence interval. No upper confidence bound is shown.",
